	METHOD a dropPendingAction (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/a/s;)V
		COMMENT Removes a single pending entry for the given action from this factory's queue, without refunding twice. CustomUnit forwards to buildQueue.a(SpecialAction), which looks the action up in the queue's secondary (pending) list, calls either e(unit, price) or d(unit, price) on its price depending on the item's k "already cancelled" flag, then drops the entry. Contrast with toggleQueuedAction(SpecialAction, boolean), the enqueue/cancel path used by the build buttons.
	METHOD a executeSpecialAction (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/a/s;Z)V
		COMMENT Executes or cancels a special action on this unit, the two-argument convenience form. CustomUnit delegates straight to a(SpecialAction, boolean, PointF, Unit) with a null target point and null target unit; the boolean is the cancel flag (false = perform, true = cancel). Base Unit declares it unchanged so subclasses such as CustomUnit and the built-in unit types can supply the semantics.
	METHOD a handleSpecialAction (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/a/s;ZLandroid/graphics/PointF;Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/am;)V
		COMMENT Core special-action handler for this unit: performs the action when the boolean is false, or cancels it when true, optionally against a target point and target unit. CustomUnit special-cases the built-in unload actions first (Hovercraft.i starts unloading, Hovercraft.j stops it), then for ExtraAction dispatches through the action config; other actions route into checkTargetedActionOrder when a target point must be validated. Callers: executeSpecialAction(SpecialAction,boolean) and the internal paths that carry a target. The Factory counterpart implements the same contract for built-in buildings.
