	METHOD aj isBuilderUnit ()Z
		COMMENT Unit-level forward of UnitTypeInterface.useAsBuilder() ([ai]useAsBuilder for custom units). OrderableUnit returns this.r().useAsBuilder(); CustomUnit returns this.meta.fq; Tree and SpreadFire return false. All three call sites are AI builder selection: Base.a(UnitTypeInterface,PointF,boolean) filters candidate builders with var10.aj(), AI.a(UnitTypeInterface) requires !aj() to qualify a unit as an attacker, and AI.n(float) only regroups/reorders idle units that pass aj(). Distinct from isBuilder() (ak), which reports [core]isBuilder.
	METHOD ak isBuilder ()Z
		COMMENT True when this unit's type is a builder ([core]isBuilder). OrderableUnit returns this.r().isBuilder(); CustomUnit returns this.meta.fp; Tree and SpreadFire return false. Callers: UnitDetectElement.isUnitCountInRange uses it verbatim as "this.onlyBuilders || var6.ak()"; Team.updateDefeatCheck and TriggerEngine.matchesObjective use "bJ() || ak()" to mean the team still has a factory or a builder (so it is not yet defeated / matches the noConstructionOrTech objective); BattleInterface.handleDragSelection drops builders from a drag box that also contains a combat unit. Distinct from isBuilderUnit() (aj), which reports the [ai]useAsBuilder role flag.
	METHOD b setTeamDirect (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/n;)V
	METHOD b toggleQueuedAction (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/a/s;Z)V
		COMMENT Toggles a queued production action for this factory, i.e. the handler behind clicking a build button. CustomUnit forwards to buildQueue.a(SpecialAction, boolean); FactoryBuildQueue then acts on QueueUnitAction entries: when the boolean is false it queues the unit (after checking precondition s.a(unit,true), the unit-count cap via getUnitsMax and affordability via price.b(unit, queue)), and when the boolean is true it removes the entry and refunds through the action's price. The empty-action overload a(SpecialAction) instead drops a pending item from the queue's secondary list. Base Unit has no implementation; the Factory counterpart does the same for built-in buildings.
