	METHOD bW getSecondaryBarFill ()F
		COMMENT Fill fraction in [0,1] of the small secondary status bar drawn under the health bar, or -1.0F for "no secondary bar". Base returns -1.0F. Consumer: Unit.drawOverlay, which draws it in blue and asks isRechargingEnergy() to pick a greyer palette while recharging. CustomUnit picks the first applicable source in order: (1) energy, currentEnergy / unitData.maxEnergy, when maxEnergy > 0, energy is below max and showEnergyBar is set; (2) shield, currentShield / maxShield, under the same conditions with showShieldBar; (3) when the unit has neither energy nor shield at all, the reload progress of meta.em (1 - reloadTimer / getTurretShootDelay) or the warmup progress of meta.en (f / getTurretWarmup).
	METHOD bX isRechargingEnergy ()Z
	METHOD bY getUsedTransportSlotsForDisplay ()I
		COMMENT Number of transport slots currently occupied, or -1 to mean "this unit is not a transport, draw no slot bar". Base returns -1. Consumer: Unit.drawOverlay, which skips the whole slot-bar block when the value is negative and otherwise fills the first getUsedTransportSlotsForDisplay() cells of the getTransportSlotsForDisplay() wide grid. Implementations: Hovercraft sums getTransportSlotsNeeded() over its transported-units list; Dropship does the same; CustomUnit returns getUsedTransportSlots() but only when maxTransportingUnits is non-zero and showTransportBar is set, otherwise -1.
	METHOD bZ getTransportSlotsForDisplay ()I
		COMMENT Total number of transport slots this unit provides, i.e. the width of the slot grid Unit.drawOverlay draws; -1 means "not a transport". Base returns -1. Hovercraft and Dropship return their fixed capacity (Hovercraft 4). CustomUnit returns maxTransportingUnits when it is non-zero and showTransportBar is set, otherwise -1. Note that drawOverlay only enters this block when getUsedTransportSlotsForDisplay() is >= 0, so the two must agree on the -1 sentinel.
