	METHOD ca drawRallyPointLine ()V
		COMMENT Draws the rally-point tether line from a factory to the point it will send newly produced units. CustomUnit draws it only when buildQueue.b (the pending rally position) is non-null, using Factory.y as the line colour. Base implementation is empty; it is invoked from Unit's selection drawing path, gated behind settings.showUnitWaypoints.
	METHOD cA getConsumedResources ()Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/custom/e/f;
	METHOD cb drawRangeUIGuides ()V
		COMMENT Draws the translucent range-helper rings shown while exactly one unit is selected. Base implementation is empty; the caller is Unit's selection drawing path, which only reaches it when GameUtils.isSingleSelectedUnit is true. CustomUnit draws, in order: (1) either the unit's attack range via getAttackRange() when the unit can attack, or - for a building that cannot attack - the unit's build range from unitData.o, both suppressed when showRangeUIGuide is explicitly false; (2) one ring per entry in meta.o (the extra range-guide list); (3) when meta.bF is set, a per-turret ring for each turret whose interceptProjectilesAndTargetingGroundUnderDistance is positive, drawn in a dimmer green when another ring was already drawn.
	METHOD cB getInternalNameWithId ()Ljava/lang/String;
