	METHOD cd getConstructionFootprint ()Landroid/graphics/Rect;
	METHOD cD getRenderScale ()F
		COMMENT Uniform scale factor applied around the unit's centre point when rendering its body sprite; 1.0F means no scaling. Consumers: OrderableUnit.draw and aQ(), which call GraphicsEngine.scaleAroundPoint(cD(), cD(), centreX, centreY) around the body/turret blit and restore afterwards. CustomUnit returns this.meta.bH * this.animScale: the loader derives meta.bH from [graphics]scaleImagesTo (divided by total_frames, times globalScale) and then multiplies it by [graphics]imageScale, while animScale is driven by AnimationKeyFrameType.scale keyframes, so the two channels compose.
	METHOD ce getDisplayFootprint ()Landroid/graphics/Rect;
	METHOD cf isVisibleToPlayer ()Z
	METHOD cF getScreenRect ()Landroid/graphics/RectF;
	METHOD cg isVisibleToAllPlayers ()Z
		COMMENT True when this unit is visible to all players, including enemies. CustomUnit returns unitData.m, a per-unit-data boolean; when it is false the unit counts as hidden from hostile players. Consumers all gate on team ownership: InterfaceEngine.canSelectUnit refuses to select an enemy unit that reads false, InterfaceEngine.getUnitAtPosition skips it during hit-testing, AI.j(Unit) filters it out of target picking, and CustomUnit.isVisibleUnit additionally hides it from an enemy viewer unless that viewer is a spectator.
	METHOD cG hasShadowFrames ()Z
		COMMENT True when the unit's spritesheet carries separate drop-shadow frames, so the renderer must blit a shadow quad instead of drawing a rotated shadow sprite. CustomUnit returns this.meta.aq, which CustomUnitMetadataLoader sets to true when the shadow image was generated as an animation strip (Unit.createShadowImage) or when [graphics]image_shadow_frames is true. Sole consumer is OrderableUnit.aQ() (the turret pass), which branches to GraphicsEngine.drawImage with a source Rect from a_(true) when true, and to drawImageRotated otherwise.
